- Okay, I like, nice song. Yeah.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:12.620
♪ Say you really want it ♪

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.650
- That's a great song.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.380
All right, so you have two
boys, eleven and seven.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.880
Oh, that's a lot of boys in the house.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.990
I only have one, and that's a lot.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.430
So, you grew up with women though, right?

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.263
- [Evangeline] Yeah.

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.234
- Just sisters.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.640
- Just sisters and just
female cousins, as well.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.900
It's just a world of estrogen.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.733
- [Kelly] Whoa.

00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:26.566
- Yeah.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:27.690
- God was just placing
a challenge before you.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.741
Yeah, with the two boys.

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:29.580
- Well, I don't know why I always knew

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.570
I was gonna have boys.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.403
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah?

00:00:31.403 --> 00:00:33.690
- Yeah, because I couldn't
deal with girls' drama ever.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:34.672
- Yeah.

00:00:34.672 --> 00:00:35.505
(audience laughing)

00:00:35.505 --> 00:00:36.360
- Never, not even when I
was a young teenage girl.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.940
- I know a couple guys
that are just chickens.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.210
They're hens. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.043
(audience laughs)

00:00:41.043 --> 00:00:42.268
- Yeah, you've made a very
good point there, Kelly.

00:00:42.268 --> 00:00:43.290
- [Kelly] Yeah, I was
like, "I know a lot of guys

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.730
that are hens that like to stir a pot."

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.046
I don't know if this is true.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.879
(Kelly chuckling)

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:47.790
- But I have to say, even as a girl,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.540
I thought that boys at this
age, like eleven and seven,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.480
especially eleven, middle
school, were so weird.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.790
I couldn't understand
them for the life of me.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.672
And as a mom now-

00:00:57.672 --> 00:00:58.560
- They're just simple.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.090
- Strange though, strange.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:00.923
- Yeah.

00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:03.120
- And as a mom now, I'm like,
I still don't understand.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:03.953
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:03.953 --> 00:01:04.860
- I don't know what's going on here,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.071
I don't understand the noises
coming out of your mouth.

00:01:07.071 --> 00:01:07.904
(audience laughing)

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:09.528
- My son is Max, from Wild
Things. He's that character.

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:11.430
- [Evangeline] My oldest
son is like that as well.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.860
Yeah. And he has this,
he makes up weird sayings

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.620
and sounds, and he just
says them over and over.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.690
He's got this one where he goes,

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.257
he says to his younger brother,

00:01:20.257 --> 00:01:23.220
"I'm sorry for touching your bum bum".

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.181
- [Kelly] That's it, no.

00:01:24.181 --> 00:01:25.014
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:26.430
Why do they love saying, they love...

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.365
My son is just like "Poop".

00:01:28.365 --> 00:01:29.198
(Everyone laughing)

00:01:29.198 --> 00:01:32.220
And I'm like, "Yep, okay."
It's like, they get,

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.495
he just loves weird words like that.

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:35.328
- Yeah.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.161
- And you're like, it's not really funny,

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:37.200
but I'll laugh with you.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.033
- For your sake.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:38.990
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:39.823
- Again, I'm having flashbacks.

00:01:39.823 --> 00:01:40.830
- I'm teaching you what the
girl's gonna do on the date,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.258
to pretend you're funny.

00:01:42.258 --> 00:01:43.091
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:43.091 --> 00:01:43.924
- Exactly.

00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:44.910
- It's like, Anyway, my son is six,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.110
so what do I have to look forward to?

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.149
He's already a little
strange, in an awesome way.

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:49.982
- Always an awesome way.

00:01:49.982 --> 00:01:51.750
- I haven't gotten into boy B.O yet.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.583
- [Evangeline] Yeah.

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:53.516
- Have you gotten into that?

00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:54.810
- No. Just a little
tiny touch, not so much.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.298
Although, the girls his age
aren't smelling so good,

00:01:57.298 --> 00:01:58.131
I've gotta tell you.

00:01:58.131 --> 00:01:58.964
- Yeah. Well, that happens.

00:01:58.964 --> 00:01:59.797
- They've gone there.

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:00.780
- Yeah.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.613
- But you do have to look forward to him

00:02:01.613 --> 00:02:06.150
thinking you are not cool
and being your worst critic.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:06.983
So, that is definitely on the way.

00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:08.290
- That's already happening.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.504
- Well, well done. Well done, you.

00:02:10.504 --> 00:02:11.337
(everyone laughing)

00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:12.170
- He is advanced.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.860
- Yes, exactly. Yeah.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.300
- Sometimes, every once in a while,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.460
I'll do something really
cool, or if I know someone.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.020
- [Evangeline] Uh-huh.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.900
I've met Owen from Jurassic
World, and he's like-

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.733
- [Evangeline] Oh.

00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:23.707
- Yeah, that's his favorite person.

00:02:23.707 --> 00:02:24.540
- [Evangeline] You're in now.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.373
- Yeah.

00:02:25.373 --> 00:02:27.940
- I thought I might be in
once I became an Avenger-

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:28.773
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:29.743
- [Evangeline] And then my son, of course-

00:02:29.743 --> 00:02:30.840
- [Kelly] How did you not, with that?

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.360
- Well, he can always find
the way that I am not cool.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.440
- I'm like, these are high standards.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.273
- I know. He was like,

00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:38.054
"Mom, why do you have to
be the worst Avenger?"

00:02:38.054 --> 00:02:39.864
(audience gasping) (Kelly laughing)

00:02:39.864 --> 00:02:40.698
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:02:40.698 --> 00:02:42.450
"Why couldn't you be Iron Man?"

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.610
And I was like, Okay.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.443
- Well.

00:02:45.443 --> 00:02:47.397
- I'm trying my very
best. Well, there's a...

00:02:47.397 --> 00:02:48.510
- Not a man.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.770
- Yeah, that helps.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.840
But then, now with Quantumania,

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.570
I've sort of, graduated
to being a senior Avenger.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.130
And he's like, "Okay
mom, now you're cool."

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.470
- Yeah. I'm like, oh my
God, that would be like...

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.490
How was the costume for you?

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.510
Because I always feel like,

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.190
when y'all wear all those
costumes, I hear everybody talk

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.810
about how uncomfortable
they are. Was yours?

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.430
- Yeah, no. I love, I mean...

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.263
- [Kelly] You loved it?

00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:07.338
- [Evangeline] I took naps in my costume.

00:03:07.338 --> 00:03:08.580
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.413
- [Kelly] I've gotta be honest with you,

00:03:09.413 --> 00:03:11.250
if I looked like that in that costume,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.459
I'd probably keep it on too.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:13.292
- (Evangeline chuckling)

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:14.190
You'd nap in it also. Yeah.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.690
- I would walk into Target like that.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.150
- I don't, honestly, I've said it before,

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.340
but I think the reason why people complain

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.280
about their costumes is
because the "people" are mostly

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.000
male "people." And they're not
used to suffering for beauty.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.125
They're not used to being, you know-

00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:29.430
- Spanx. They're not used to all that.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.353
- Like corseted into a gown.

00:03:31.353 --> 00:03:32.186
- Yeah.

00:03:32.186 --> 00:03:33.019
- We're like-

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:34.577
- Welcome to the dark side fellas.

00:03:34.577 --> 00:03:35.410
(everyone laughing)

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.750
Yeah, it's uncomfortable.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.280
- Welcome to leather and corsets.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.315
- Yeah, try birth. Okay.

00:03:40.315 --> 00:03:41.148
(audience applauding)

00:03:41.148 --> 00:03:43.350
- So you live in Hawaii
now, and I have to ask,

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.420
this was the most beautiful
footage I've ever seen.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.370
Do butterflies just land
on people all the time?

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.420
Look at this footage.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.837
That's a real butterfly just
hanging out on her head!

00:03:49.837 --> 00:03:51.390
(Evangeline laughing)

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.510
And you're so peaceful and zen about it.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.910
In the video there's music
playing and it's like-

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.640
- Can I tell you how much that tickled?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.473
(audience laughing)

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.306
That was-

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:02.139
- [Kelly] How do you not wipe it away.

00:04:02.139 --> 00:04:06.000
- I could feel the little
feet grabbing my eyelids,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.430
and plucking away at them,

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.160
but it was just too cool of an
opportunity not to stay still

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:11.993
and let it cruise.

00:04:11.993 --> 00:04:12.826
- [Kelly] It's so cool.

00:04:12.826 --> 00:04:13.659
- It happens all of the time.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:15.030
I mean, everyone in Hawaii has butterflies

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.973
in their face all the time.

00:04:15.973 --> 00:04:16.950
(audience laughing)

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:17.880
- That's not true.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.008
- No, it's totally true.

00:04:19.008 --> 00:04:19.841
- (chuckling) It's not.

00:04:19.841 --> 00:04:21.360
- Life out there is Snow
White and the seven dwarves.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.193
- Are you serious?

00:04:22.193 --> 00:04:23.845
- Well, except I only have
two doors and a husband.

00:04:23.845 --> 00:04:25.101
- [Kelly] Yes. Yes.

00:04:25.101 --> 00:04:25.934
(audience laughing)

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:26.767
- But, same idea.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:27.600
- [Kelly] You're working on it.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.470
I just thought that was so peaceful.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.407
Again, I was like, you have found balance-

00:04:30.407 --> 00:04:31.240
(Evangeline laughing)

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.090
when that can happen in your life.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.760
But also when you were younger,
you were a flight attendant.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.440
So how did, I didn't know
that. So how did that...

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.600
How were people? I feel like
that's one of the worst jobs.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.950
People, you get people in grumpy spaces.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.730
- Well, you gotta remember
this was 25 years ago.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:45.596
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:45.596 --> 00:04:47.910
- (chuckling) People were
so much nicer 25 years ago.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:48.743
- That is totally true.

00:04:48.743 --> 00:04:49.950
- People are miserable now.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:50.783
- Okay.

00:04:50.783 --> 00:04:51.674
- [Evangeline] Yeah, they're miserable.

00:04:51.674 --> 00:04:52.507
- Maybe they were faking
it back then, though.

00:04:52.507 --> 00:04:53.357
- Well, yeah.

00:04:53.357 --> 00:04:54.350
- Maybe they're just
honest now. (chuckling)

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.040
- But you know, every once in
a while there would be that

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.010
flyer that was miserable and mean,

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:02.220
and unkind and deserving
of some sort of punishment.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.670
And so the real only punishment
I had at my disposal was

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.860
a little flyby crop dusting.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:09.693
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:05:09.693 --> 00:05:11.010
just a little boop, just a little boop.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.290
And then just keep going.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.123
And they'd be like, "Oh,
who did that to me?"

00:05:14.123 --> 00:05:16.290
- (chuckling) Crop
dusting. That's a good one.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.647
And I'd be like, "Not me. What?"

00:05:17.647 --> 00:05:18.480
- [Kelly] What?

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.313
- "Not me."

00:05:19.313 --> 00:05:20.146
- [Kelly] Not little old me.

00:05:20.146 --> 00:05:20.979
- "I'm just a fly attendant."

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:22.294
- You're just tooting.

00:05:22.294 --> 00:05:23.127
(everyone laughing)

00:05:23.127 --> 00:05:24.870
- Past the grumpy guy,
which is probably making

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.670
him even more grump, which
is winning. You're winning.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:27.503
- Which is so winning.

00:05:27.503 --> 00:05:28.419
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:29.252
- And I love that you said "tooting."

00:05:29.252 --> 00:05:30.085
- [Kelly] Tooting. I know.

00:05:30.085 --> 00:05:31.920
I just love that you were
crop dusting passengers.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.180
We would've been friends.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.320
- We totally are now.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.000
- [Kelly] That is already funny.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.100
So wait, we were talking
about your kids before,

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.999
and you have this kids
book. This is awesome.

00:05:39.999 --> 00:05:40.832
- I do.

00:05:40.832 --> 00:05:41.665
What can you tell us about them?

00:05:41.665 --> 00:05:42.900
What made you wanna do
this? This is awesome.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.390
- Well, I was a little
kid who hated reading,

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.730
because the books were always
too long and too wordy.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.930
And I was a very slow reader.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:49.763
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:49.763 --> 00:05:51.390
- But then the ones that
were short and sweet

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.580
and had great illustrations
were just kiddie stuff,

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.680
and they were boring and they
weren't sophisticated enough.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.599
- Yeah.

00:05:56.599 --> 00:05:57.432
- So I was like, I'm gonna make the book

00:05:57.432 --> 00:05:59.100
that I would've wanted
to read when I was a kid.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.943
- That's the smartest thing to
do, something you would want.

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:01.776
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:01.776 --> 00:06:03.240
- Yeah. And then I call
them cautionary tales

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.893
for modern day brats, because-

00:06:06.182 --> 00:06:07.015
(everyone laughing)

00:06:07.015 --> 00:06:07.848
Because our kids have become brats,

00:06:07.848 --> 00:06:09.660
cause we don't tell these
stories to them anymore.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:10.696
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:10.696 --> 00:06:11.715
- Which are like, just so you know-

00:06:11.715 --> 00:06:12.548
- [Kelly] Like warnings.

00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:15.000
- If you're a jerk, your
life might not go so well.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:15.833
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:16.709
- That's just reality.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:17.730
- You could die like the evil queen.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.563
- [Evangeline] Yeah, exactly.

00:06:18.563 --> 00:06:20.370
- You could get put in an
oven like the evil witch.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.480
- Yeah, exactly.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:22.680
- You might get burned-

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:23.513
- [Kelly] Let's scar them. (chuckling)

00:06:23.513 --> 00:06:24.346
- Yes. Those are important things to do.

00:06:24.346 --> 00:06:26.220
- Fairy tales are scary, but they do have

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.930
amazing life lessons.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.640
- And I call them for modern day brats,

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.340
cause they're not that same shaming thing.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.232
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:33.232 --> 00:06:34.530
- They're just like,
they're gently cautionary.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.110
And there's always, in the
end, a redemptive story,

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.280
which is essentially like

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.490
in our worst failures
is when we can wake up

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.371
and realize how to do better next time.

00:06:42.371 --> 00:06:43.980
- [Kelly] Yeah. Absolutely.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.872
- Yeah.

00:06:44.872 --> 00:06:46.050
- And teaching them that
failure is a reality.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:46.883
- Yeah.

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:47.716
- We're not always gonna win.

00:06:47.716 --> 00:06:49.200
- And for those parents
who are too afraid to

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.420
actually let their children really lose,

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.421
which is clearly not us-

00:06:52.421 --> 00:06:54.137
- [Kelly] You're hurting them. Yeah.

00:06:54.137 --> 00:06:54.970
Clearly. (chuckling)

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.540
- Clearly. This is a really
